1
00:00:02,676 --> 00:00:05,679
My name is Chinatsu Kano.
Thanks for having me.

2
00:00:05,762 --> 00:00:07,931
[all] Welcome to the Inomata household!

3
00:00:08,473 --> 00:00:09,808
I have a little something.

4
00:00:09,891 --> 00:00:11,935
[Taiki's mom] Gosh,
you didn't have to do that.

5
00:00:12,519 --> 00:00:14,438
{\an8}She's really beautiful, isn't she?

6
00:00:14,521 --> 00:00:16,982
{\an8}Looks just like
your grandmother did, Taiki.

7
00:00:17,524 --> 00:00:20,193
{\an8}Isn't this nice, son?
She really livens up the place.

8
00:00:21,737 --> 00:00:23,947
[Taiki] <i>That's a major understatement.</i>

9
00:00:24,031 --> 00:00:28,201
<i>I'm already losing it just from
seeing Chinatsu in regular clothes.</i>

10
00:00:28,785 --> 00:00:30,704
<i>There she is. On our stairs.</i>

11
00:00:31,329 --> 00:00:33,206
<i>In our kitchen with my mom.</i>

12
00:00:33,832 --> 00:00:35,459
<i>She's even eating sushi!</i>

13
00:00:36,418 --> 00:00:38,962
<i>How am I going to make it through this?</i>

14
00:00:40,172 --> 00:00:42,174
[opening theme song playing]

15
00:00:43,216 --> 00:00:46,428
BLUE BOX

16
00:02:02,671 --> 00:02:08,927
BLUE BOX

17
00:02:09,010 --> 00:02:11,221
{\an8}[Taiki] <i>So this is my life
for the next two years?</i>

18
00:02:11,304 --> 00:02:12,848
{\an8}EPISODE 2
YOU HAVE TO GO TO NATIONALS

19
00:02:12,931 --> 00:02:14,683
{\an8}<i>This won't end until she graduates?</i>

20
00:02:14,766 --> 00:02:15,725
[cheering]

21
00:02:15,809 --> 00:02:19,312
<i>I was pumped the other day
just for advancing to the second round.</i>

22
00:02:19,896 --> 00:02:23,817
<i>But living under the same roof?
It's like competing in the Olympics.</i>

23
00:02:23,900 --> 00:02:25,694
[knocking at door]

24
00:02:26,194 --> 00:02:27,070
[Chinatsu] Taiki.

25
00:02:27,571 --> 00:02:28,905
[funky music playing]

26
00:02:28,989 --> 00:02:31,700
Um, your mom told me to tell you
that the bath is free.

27
00:02:31,783 --> 00:02:32,951
[exclaims]

28
00:02:34,327 --> 00:02:35,453
[Taiki] <i>Loungewear?</i>

29
00:02:35,537 --> 00:02:39,457
<i>And straight out of the bath,
she's glowing even more than usual.</i>

30
00:02:40,125 --> 00:02:42,002
{\an8}I'll go when I'm done reading this!

31
00:02:42,085 --> 00:02:45,213
{\an8}[gasps] Oh, my gosh, no way.
That isn't this week's <i>Jump,</i> is it?

32
00:02:45,297 --> 00:02:46,256
[Taiki] What the--

33
00:02:46,339 --> 00:02:48,800
{\an8}[Chinatsu] I've been running around
so much with the move,

34
00:02:48,884 --> 00:02:51,636
{\an8}I haven't gotten
to read this week's latest one.

35
00:02:51,720 --> 00:02:52,596
{\an8}[Taiki] <i>So close!</i>

36
00:02:53,263 --> 00:02:55,056
Why don't I lend you my copy!

37
00:02:55,140 --> 00:02:56,850
- Really?
- Yeah, of course!

38
00:02:58,018 --> 00:03:00,687
<i>If she comes any closer, I'm in trouble.</i>

39
00:03:00,770 --> 00:03:01,605
Huh?

40
00:03:03,440 --> 00:03:05,150
What's going on?

41
00:03:05,233 --> 00:03:07,611
Hm. I'm just relieved.

42
00:03:08,528 --> 00:03:12,115
It's been nerve wracking
living in another person's home.

43
00:03:12,782 --> 00:03:16,620
Our parents may be good friends,
but I've only met yours a couple times.

44
00:03:17,412 --> 00:03:20,957
So having a familiar face around
from morning practice like you,

45
00:03:21,041 --> 00:03:23,251
you letting me borrow your manga...

46
00:03:24,794 --> 00:03:26,296
I feel more at home.

47
00:03:27,881 --> 00:03:29,466
[Taiki] <i>More at home?</i>

48
00:03:30,467 --> 00:03:31,760
{\an8}All right, goodnight.

49
00:03:37,224 --> 00:03:40,644
[Taiki's psyche] <i>Feelings of guilt...</i>

50
00:03:42,354 --> 00:03:45,106
[Taiki] <i>At the end of the day,
I'm still just a guy.</i>

51
00:03:45,982 --> 00:03:46,858
[unzipping]

52
00:03:46,942 --> 00:03:50,195
<i>Is she not even fazed
by the thought of living with...</i>

53
00:03:50,278 --> 00:03:51,696
<i>a guy her age?</i>

54
00:03:52,489 --> 00:03:53,657
[exclaiming]

55
00:03:57,535 --> 00:04:00,538
[exclaims]

56
00:04:02,916 --> 00:04:06,419
<i>Because if she isn't,
then I'm being an idiot for no reason.</i>

57
00:04:08,505 --> 00:04:10,465
[yells]

58
00:04:10,548 --> 00:04:12,175
[quirky music playing]

59
00:04:12,259 --> 00:04:13,343
Let's go!

60
00:04:13,426 --> 00:04:15,845
[Kyo] Where did all this
upbeat energy come from?

61
00:04:15,929 --> 00:04:17,931
Aren't you supposed to be moping around?

62
00:04:18,014 --> 00:04:20,058
I'm allowed to be happy
when things are good.

63
00:04:20,141 --> 00:04:22,310
Look, I understand that you're hyped,

64
00:04:22,394 --> 00:04:25,313
but make sure people don't find out
you're living together.

65
00:04:25,397 --> 00:04:28,400
- What?
- [Kyo] Don't "what" me. Look over there.

66
00:04:31,486 --> 00:04:32,988
She's so awesome.

67
00:04:33,071 --> 00:04:35,282
Not there, guys.
Get the camera to zoom out.

68
00:04:36,950 --> 00:04:38,285
[exclaims]

69
00:04:38,368 --> 00:04:41,371
[Kyo] I tried to tell you already,
Chinatsu is super popular.

70
00:04:42,539 --> 00:04:44,499
And if any of those guys found out...

71
00:04:44,582 --> 00:04:47,085
[boy] <i>Don't move now, basketball hoop.</i>

72
00:04:47,168 --> 00:04:49,421
[Taiki grunts]

73
00:04:49,504 --> 00:04:50,505
[quirky music ends]

74
00:04:50,588 --> 00:04:52,507
Regardless, consider yourself lucky.

75
00:04:53,174 --> 00:04:55,010
Even though your parents decided,

76
00:04:55,093 --> 00:04:57,012
you get to live with someone you like.

77
00:04:57,095 --> 00:04:59,264
So you might end up dating after all.

78
00:04:59,931 --> 00:05:01,057
[Taiki] No way, dude.

79
00:05:01,141 --> 00:05:03,685
She chose to stay behind
in Japan on her own.

80
00:05:04,519 --> 00:05:08,732
She's so dead-set on sports,
throwing in a, "Hey, wanna go out?" now...

81
00:05:08,815 --> 00:05:09,941
not an option.

82
00:05:10,984 --> 00:05:12,444
So after thinking about it,

83
00:05:13,278 --> 00:05:15,697
I want to go
to nationals this summer, too.

84
00:05:15,780 --> 00:05:16,948
[grunts]

85
00:05:17,032 --> 00:05:18,283
[Kyo] Dude.

86
00:05:19,492 --> 00:05:20,827
[Taiki] I have to,

87
00:05:20,910 --> 00:05:23,496
it's the only chance I have
of getting on her level.

88
00:05:23,580 --> 00:05:24,831
[pants]

89
00:05:24,914 --> 00:05:26,166
You are aware

90
00:05:26,249 --> 00:05:29,961
that you've got a slim chance of making it
to nationals in your first year?

91
00:05:30,045 --> 00:05:32,547
Given your current skills,
it may be impossible--

92
00:05:32,630 --> 00:05:34,382
Maybe you're right, maybe not...

93
00:05:35,800 --> 00:05:37,469
But it won't stop me from trying!

94
00:05:38,511 --> 00:05:39,637
[sighs]

95
00:05:40,221 --> 00:05:42,348
So come on, play me again!

96
00:05:42,432 --> 00:05:44,642
Resting is a key part of training.

97
00:05:44,726 --> 00:05:45,894
What?

98
00:05:45,977 --> 00:05:48,897
- [Nishida] Taiki! I'll take you on!
- [Taiki] All right!

99
00:05:49,564 --> 00:05:52,150
Huh? He's playing someone else now?

100
00:05:53,026 --> 00:05:55,445
Hasn't he been playing the whole practice?

101
00:05:55,528 --> 00:05:58,490
Once he sets his mind on something,
there's no stopping him.

102
00:05:58,573 --> 00:05:59,783
What's he set on?

103
00:05:59,866 --> 00:06:02,118
Apparently, he wants to go
to nationals this year.

104
00:06:02,202 --> 00:06:03,411
And...

105
00:06:04,120 --> 00:06:05,455
Do you think he can?

106
00:06:05,538 --> 00:06:07,165
- Uh...
- [chuckles]

107
00:06:07,248 --> 00:06:10,001
It's just, he always pushes himself.

108
00:06:10,627 --> 00:06:11,753
[giggles]

109
00:06:12,712 --> 00:06:14,422
[Kyo] Well, at the end of the day,

110
00:06:14,506 --> 00:06:17,133
those who go after what they want
are usually the strongest...

111
00:06:18,426 --> 00:06:20,136
in everything they do.

112
00:06:20,220 --> 00:06:21,930
- [clattering]
- [Taiki] Forty-five.

113
00:06:22,013 --> 00:06:23,348
Forty-six.

114
00:06:23,431 --> 00:06:24,641
Forty-seven.

115
00:06:24,724 --> 00:06:25,975
WORKOUT ROUTINE

116
00:06:26,059 --> 00:06:27,936
Forty-eight. Forty-nine.

117
00:06:28,019 --> 00:06:30,105
[straining] Fifty!

118
00:06:30,688 --> 00:06:32,398
[grunting]

119
00:06:34,359 --> 00:06:35,401
[Taiki] <i>I'm beat.</i>

120
00:06:36,569 --> 00:06:39,155
<i>But... I gotta keep at it.</i>

121
00:06:39,239 --> 00:06:41,241
<i>Playing like this
won't get me to nationals.</i>

122
00:06:41,324 --> 00:06:44,661
<i>A dream will stay a dream
if you don't wake up, Taiki!</i>

123
00:06:45,286 --> 00:06:46,371
[Chinatsu] Uh...

124
00:06:46,454 --> 00:06:47,914
[Taiki] <i>Chinatsu!</i>

125
00:06:47,997 --> 00:06:49,541
What are you watching?

126
00:06:49,624 --> 00:06:51,543
Oh, you know, just... something dumb!

127
00:06:53,002 --> 00:06:56,172
I had someone film me playing,
so I was watching it to see my form.

128
00:06:56,256 --> 00:06:57,799
- Show me!
- What?

129
00:06:58,508 --> 00:07:01,052
- No way. It's too embarrassing!
- Oh, come on.

130
00:07:01,970 --> 00:07:03,805
I watch you practice all the time anyway.

131
00:07:05,348 --> 00:07:08,059
[Taiki] <i>And here I thought
I was the only one watching.</i>

132
00:07:08,143 --> 00:07:09,477
[mellow music playing]

133
00:07:09,561 --> 00:07:10,812
Wow, you're so good.

134
00:07:11,563 --> 00:07:15,567
Being able to react to a birdie that fast,
and flying around the court like that...

135
00:07:16,109 --> 00:07:18,820
No way. I still move too slow.

136
00:07:19,487 --> 00:07:21,364
My first step needs to be faster,

137
00:07:21,448 --> 00:07:23,491
or my shots won't be as accurate.

138
00:07:23,575 --> 00:07:25,034
I'm barely keeping up.

139
00:07:25,118 --> 00:07:27,287
I need to be collected
to make those shots.

140
00:07:28,455 --> 00:07:31,332
I'll never get
to nationals like this. [gasps]

141
00:07:32,167 --> 00:07:33,084
Wait nationals?

142
00:07:33,585 --> 00:07:35,920
Err. No, I meant like, uh...

143
00:07:36,463 --> 00:07:38,715
<i>I had decided I wouldn't tell her...</i>

144
00:07:38,798 --> 00:07:41,342
<i>until it felt like
I had a shot at making it.</i>

145
00:07:41,968 --> 00:07:43,511
- You said it.
- Huh?

146
00:07:43,595 --> 00:07:45,597
So you're going to nationals,
then, huh, Taiki?

147
00:07:45,680 --> 00:07:48,266
Huh? I meant something else.

148
00:07:48,349 --> 00:07:49,601
What, you're not going?

149
00:07:49,684 --> 00:07:51,603
Even though you just said it out loud?

150
00:07:52,187 --> 00:07:54,439
[breathing heavily] Please, Chinatsu.

151
00:07:54,522 --> 00:07:57,525
You have... to go to nationals.

152
00:07:57,609 --> 00:08:01,029
[grunts] I'll go. I'm going to nationals!

153
00:08:01,112 --> 00:08:02,530
<i>Ah, man.</i>

154
00:08:02,614 --> 00:08:05,950
<i>Why do I always come off
as such a doofus around her?</i>

155
00:08:06,951 --> 00:08:07,952
Hold on just a sec.

156
00:08:08,036 --> 00:08:08,870
[mellow music ends]

157
00:08:14,626 --> 00:08:16,377
Take this, if you want.

158
00:08:16,920 --> 00:08:18,129
[Taiki] A wish bracelet?

159
00:08:18,213 --> 00:08:21,508
I made this one
when I decided to stay in Japan.

160
00:08:21,591 --> 00:08:23,009
As a wish, I guess.

161
00:08:23,092 --> 00:08:25,637
I was hoping it would
help me feel more courageous.

162
00:08:26,721 --> 00:08:28,431
If you don't like it, that's o--

163
00:08:29,933 --> 00:08:30,892
I am honored!

164
00:08:31,518 --> 00:08:34,687
<i>She gave me something!
And she made it with her own two hands!</i>

165
00:08:34,771 --> 00:08:36,898
<i>I will treasure it till the end of time.</i>

166
00:08:37,649 --> 00:08:39,651
[Chinatsu] You'll cut off
the blood flow like that.

167
00:08:39,734 --> 00:08:40,818
[gasps softly]

168
00:08:41,736 --> 00:08:43,196
[romantic music playing]

169
00:08:46,533 --> 00:08:47,700
Taiki...

170
00:08:48,785 --> 00:08:49,827
{\an8}you have to...

171
00:08:50,453 --> 00:08:51,412
{\an8}go to nationals.

172
00:08:53,081 --> 00:08:53,915
Ta-da.

173
00:08:54,582 --> 00:08:55,416
Look.

174
00:08:56,000 --> 00:08:57,168
We match.

175
00:08:59,337 --> 00:09:00,922
Don't be too careful with it.

176
00:09:02,173 --> 00:09:03,174
Night!

177
00:09:03,758 --> 00:09:05,218
Good night, Chinatsu.

178
00:09:06,803 --> 00:09:08,096
<i>Let's do this.</i>

179
00:09:08,179 --> 00:09:09,681
<i>I'll work till this falls off.</i>

180
00:09:10,473 --> 00:09:11,933
<i>That's the thought, but...</i>

181
00:09:12,016 --> 00:09:13,685
[groans]

182
00:09:13,768 --> 00:09:15,186
<i>This only...</i>

183
00:09:15,270 --> 00:09:17,480
<i>makes me like her even more.</i>

184
00:09:21,234 --> 00:09:25,488
<i>Every time I start daydreaming about her,
I'll do 30 sit-ups.</i>

185
00:09:26,489 --> 00:09:28,533
[birds chirping]

186
00:09:30,618 --> 00:09:33,037
Oh. You're leaving already?

187
00:09:33,121 --> 00:09:35,707
It's spring break,
and you're still going early?

188
00:09:35,790 --> 00:09:38,042
I'm a newbie,
so I get the set up grunt work.

189
00:09:38,710 --> 00:09:40,420
<i>Plus, I need to practice, too.</i>

190
00:09:41,963 --> 00:09:43,172
Have a good day!

191
00:09:43,256 --> 00:09:44,841
You... have a day, too.

192
00:09:49,220 --> 00:09:52,223
<i>It felt like we were married for a second.</i>

193
00:09:54,309 --> 00:09:55,852
What are you doing?

194
00:09:55,935 --> 00:09:58,438
Keeping distractions at bay! [grunts]

195
00:09:58,521 --> 00:09:59,856
[Hina] Distractions?

196
00:10:00,607 --> 00:10:02,692
The preliminaries are coming up soon.

197
00:10:03,359 --> 00:10:05,111
I gotta stay focused.

198
00:10:05,695 --> 00:10:09,073
Don't tell me, something went down
between you and basketball girl.

199
00:10:09,157 --> 00:10:10,158
[exclaims]

200
00:10:10,700 --> 00:10:12,493
- [groans]
- Is that it?

201
00:10:12,577 --> 00:10:13,995
[cheerful music playing]

202
00:10:14,579 --> 00:10:15,913
So what happened?

203
00:10:15,997 --> 00:10:17,290
Nothing.

204
00:10:17,373 --> 00:10:19,459
Did you get into her phone or something?

205
00:10:19,542 --> 00:10:20,501
I'm not a stalker.

206
00:10:21,085 --> 00:10:22,211
<i>This is bad.</i>

207
00:10:22,295 --> 00:10:26,049
<i>If Hina figures out we live together,
it'll be all kinds of trouble.</i>

208
00:10:26,132 --> 00:10:28,051
What a development in your love story!

209
00:10:28,551 --> 00:10:32,680
Let me tell you, this is a grand tale,
the story of one man's quest for love.

210
00:10:32,764 --> 00:10:34,265
He played badminton, and she...

211
00:10:34,349 --> 00:10:36,392
- [boy 1] <i>Is that him?</i>
- [boy 2] <i>Yeah, that's the guy.</i>

212
00:10:37,018 --> 00:10:39,896
[Taiki] <i>I have to keep this
under wraps no matter what.</i>

213
00:10:45,318 --> 00:10:47,528
- You left your wallet at home.
- [screams]

214
00:10:48,154 --> 00:10:50,031
I thought I dropped it somewhere!

215
00:10:50,114 --> 00:10:52,283
Thank you very much
for returning it to me!

216
00:10:52,367 --> 00:10:54,327
- [Chinatsu] Uh...
- [grunts nervously]

217
00:10:56,663 --> 00:10:57,914
{\an8}You're welcome, happy to help.

218
00:11:02,085 --> 00:11:03,169
[Taiki] <i>Was I a bit...</i>

219
00:11:03,878 --> 00:11:05,046
<i>rude just now?</i>

220
00:11:06,255 --> 00:11:09,592
[Hina] <i>Wow, you can talk to her now?
You've come so far.</i>

221
00:11:10,968 --> 00:11:12,553
{\an8}[Taiki] <i>This twerp.</i>

222
00:11:13,930 --> 00:11:16,641
That kind of thing
is just not a strong point for you.

223
00:11:17,350 --> 00:11:20,937
You should've just told her you wanted
to keep living together a secret.

224
00:11:21,020 --> 00:11:22,772
That is the least of my worries.

225
00:11:23,773 --> 00:11:24,899
This is bad, right?

226
00:11:24,982 --> 00:11:29,278
Is it bad to, I don't know,
have someone avoid you out of nowhere?

227
00:11:29,862 --> 00:11:31,447
You wanting to keep it a secret

228
00:11:31,531 --> 00:11:34,450
may've made her think
you don't like living with her.

229
00:11:34,534 --> 00:11:35,576
Or worse,

230
00:11:35,660 --> 00:11:39,247
she could be wondering if you don't want
anything to do with her at all.

231
00:11:41,749 --> 00:11:43,543
[Taiki] <i>It's actually
the complete opposite!</i>

232
00:11:43,626 --> 00:11:45,545
PRIVILEGE OF GETTING TO SEE
SENPAI'S SLEEPY SIDE

233
00:11:45,628 --> 00:11:46,796
Both of you!

234
00:11:47,463 --> 00:11:48,756
What is it, sir?

235
00:11:48,840 --> 00:11:50,425
Help me carry these, would you?

236
00:11:51,217 --> 00:11:53,719
They're for next week's entrance ceremony.

237
00:11:53,803 --> 00:11:55,888
[Taiki] We'll be taking part, actually.

238
00:11:55,972 --> 00:11:58,099
[teacher] No, I need you to take them all.

239
00:11:58,182 --> 00:12:01,185
- [Taiki] <i>He's not listening.</i>
- I need you two to help as well.

240
00:12:01,269 --> 00:12:02,186
[Hina exclaims]

241
00:12:02,270 --> 00:12:04,605
[teacher] Okay, athletes.
I'm counting on you.

242
00:12:04,689 --> 00:12:05,690
[Kyo grunts]

243
00:12:06,524 --> 00:12:08,693
[Taiki] <i>I need to straighten
this out with her ASAP.</i>

244
00:12:08,776 --> 00:12:10,695
<i>I don't want her
to take this the wrong way,</i>

245
00:12:10,778 --> 00:12:12,780
<i>and think I want nothing to do with her.</i>

246
00:12:14,031 --> 00:12:17,076
Um... I can carry one of those for you.

247
00:12:19,120 --> 00:12:20,204
I'm good.

248
00:12:20,288 --> 00:12:23,082
[Taiki] <i>Oh god, she is even angrier
than I had feared!</i>

249
00:12:23,666 --> 00:12:25,835
- [Chinatsu] Is the main entrance okay?
- Yep.

250
00:12:26,461 --> 00:12:30,214
[Taiki] <i>It's fine, she probably picked up
on needing to act like a stranger.</i>

251
00:12:30,298 --> 00:12:33,843
<i>She's not gonna hate me
because of what happened earlier, right?</i>

252
00:12:35,511 --> 00:12:36,846
<i>Why are you enjoying this?</i>

253
00:12:37,388 --> 00:12:38,556
[playful music playing]

254
00:12:38,639 --> 00:12:40,600
Um, you're Chinatsu, right?

255
00:12:40,683 --> 00:12:41,642
Yeah.

256
00:12:41,726 --> 00:12:44,353
- Do you mind if I ask you a question?
- No.

257
00:12:44,437 --> 00:12:47,356
Do you have someone special
in your life, like a boyfriend?

258
00:12:47,440 --> 00:12:49,859
- [Taiki] <i>You idiot!</i>
- No, no boyfriend.

259
00:12:50,485 --> 00:12:53,529
How can she act so casual
about something like that?

260
00:12:53,613 --> 00:12:55,990
That's not a question
you ask an upperclassman.

261
00:12:56,073 --> 00:12:59,368
- Look, dude. She's a gymnast.
- What does that even mean!

262
00:13:00,119 --> 00:13:02,121
But wait, wouldn't you like a boyfriend?

263
00:13:02,705 --> 00:13:04,665
<i>You can walk home together.</i>

264
00:13:04,749 --> 00:13:06,209
<i>Go out together.</i>

265
00:13:08,544 --> 00:13:10,713
Right now,
I'm pretty focused on basketball.

266
00:13:11,797 --> 00:13:13,382
[Hina trembling nervously]

267
00:13:14,133 --> 00:13:17,220
[Taiki] <i>You asked the question.
Stop looking so uncomfortable.</i>

268
00:13:17,303 --> 00:13:18,304
[playful music ends]

269
00:13:18,387 --> 00:13:19,597
<i>And anyway...</i>

270
00:13:19,680 --> 00:13:22,099
<i>I knew that was going to be her answer.</i>

271
00:13:27,271 --> 00:13:28,981
Oh! You're club members, right?

272
00:13:29,941 --> 00:13:31,651
Look at you here on spring break.

273
00:13:31,734 --> 00:13:34,403
Yeah, we got recruited
to help out with errands today!

274
00:13:34,487 --> 00:13:35,738
What an impressive group.

275
00:13:36,405 --> 00:13:37,532
Oh, Inomata.

276
00:13:37,615 --> 00:13:39,492
Coach Yuasa was singing your praises.

277
00:13:40,159 --> 00:13:42,495
He said your shots have developed
a lot of power recently.

278
00:13:42,578 --> 00:13:44,247
Wait, he said that?

279
00:13:44,330 --> 00:13:45,331
Yeah!

280
00:13:45,414 --> 00:13:48,000
He said you're looking good
to play at the high school level.

281
00:13:48,084 --> 00:13:52,463
And that you have a good shot at making
the team for the next national qualifiers.

282
00:13:52,547 --> 00:13:55,383
[exclaims] <i>Did you hear that, Chinatsu?</i>

283
00:13:55,466 --> 00:13:57,385
<i>She's quick to head back.</i>

284
00:14:00,221 --> 00:14:03,057
[Hina whispers] Hey, really,
did something happen between those two?

285
00:14:03,140 --> 00:14:04,892
She's giving him the cold shoulder.

286
00:14:05,977 --> 00:14:06,936
I was just thinking

287
00:14:07,019 --> 00:14:09,397
that they suit each other better
than I thought.

288
00:14:10,022 --> 00:14:11,148
[exclaims]

289
00:14:11,232 --> 00:14:12,817
[rackets whooshing]

290
00:14:12,900 --> 00:14:14,068
[grunts]

291
00:14:14,986 --> 00:14:16,696
He's really going for it.

292
00:14:16,779 --> 00:14:18,906
High school is
just around the corner for him.

293
00:14:19,574 --> 00:14:21,075
Thank you for the match!

294
00:14:22,994 --> 00:14:23,953
<i>I don't know.</i>

295
00:14:24,036 --> 00:14:26,664
<i>I thought about it,
and I'm starting to feel annoyed.</i>

296
00:14:27,248 --> 00:14:28,499
<i>I wish...</i>

297
00:14:28,583 --> 00:14:30,126
<i>I could talk about it.</i>

298
00:14:30,209 --> 00:14:32,420
<i>- Maybe even go around bragging about it.</i>
- [thuds]

299
00:14:32,503 --> 00:14:33,421
Huh?

300
00:14:37,008 --> 00:14:38,509
Hey, are you okay?

301
00:14:38,593 --> 00:14:39,427
Yeah.

302
00:14:39,510 --> 00:14:41,387
I can tell you're worried.

303
00:14:41,470 --> 00:14:43,347
But you can't go check on her, right?

304
00:14:43,431 --> 00:14:45,433
You're just strangers to one another.

305
00:14:47,018 --> 00:14:48,185
Well, that's just mean.

306
00:14:52,064 --> 00:14:53,774
[footsteps approaching]

307
00:14:54,859 --> 00:14:55,943
[Taiki] Are you okay?

308
00:14:56,027 --> 00:14:57,111
{\an8}[exclaims softly]

309
00:14:57,194 --> 00:14:59,113
Because I saw you fall earlier.

310
00:14:59,655 --> 00:15:00,948
Yes, I'm all right, but...

311
00:15:01,824 --> 00:15:05,202
{\an8}aren't you supposed to be pretending
that you and I don't know each other?

312
00:15:06,871 --> 00:15:10,207
[Taiki] I'm sorry about that.
Acting like that out of the blue.

313
00:15:11,083 --> 00:15:15,046
I guess I still feel a little awkward
about living together.

314
00:15:15,129 --> 00:15:17,965
And people pay attention to you
more than you realize.

315
00:15:18,591 --> 00:15:21,677
If word got out,
people would make up crazy stories.

316
00:15:21,761 --> 00:15:24,055
I worried you wouldn't be able
to focus on your club.

317
00:15:24,138 --> 00:15:25,932
- That's why I did it.
- What?

318
00:15:26,015 --> 00:15:27,224
That was the reason?

319
00:15:27,308 --> 00:15:29,226
What other reason would I have?

320
00:15:29,310 --> 00:15:30,311
A-ha.

321
00:15:30,394 --> 00:15:31,354
I figured...

322
00:15:31,979 --> 00:15:33,898
that it was because
you have a crush on the girl

323
00:15:33,981 --> 00:15:35,608
who's on the rhythmic gymnastics team.

324
00:15:36,609 --> 00:15:37,610
What?

325
00:15:38,486 --> 00:15:41,364
When you started acting
like you didn't know me, she was there.

326
00:15:41,989 --> 00:15:43,074
[Taiki] That was...

327
00:15:43,157 --> 00:15:44,951
[Chinatsu] I thought
the reason she asked me

328
00:15:45,034 --> 00:15:47,620
if I had a boyfriend
was because she liked you,

329
00:15:47,703 --> 00:15:49,830
and so she was trying to see how I felt.

330
00:15:50,998 --> 00:15:54,251
I'd understand wanting to hide us
living together from someone you liked.

331
00:15:54,919 --> 00:15:58,506
I was going to just keep away from you,
so no one would catch on.

332
00:15:58,589 --> 00:16:01,050
If it comes to it,
I can sleep in the shed.

333
00:16:01,133 --> 00:16:03,886
Or I could probably find
a cheap apartment somewhere.

334
00:16:04,512 --> 00:16:06,639
[Taiki] <i>So everything up to now...</i>

335
00:16:06,722 --> 00:16:09,558
<i>is 'cause she was looking out
for me and Hina?</i>

336
00:16:10,184 --> 00:16:12,645
<i>Oh man. She's adorable.</i>

337
00:16:13,229 --> 00:16:14,897
[laughs] That's stupid, Chinatsu.

338
00:16:14,981 --> 00:16:16,065
[exclaims]

339
00:16:16,148 --> 00:16:17,191
[peaceful music playing]

340
00:16:17,274 --> 00:16:18,401
[grunts softly]

341
00:16:18,484 --> 00:16:19,902
[laughing]

342
00:16:19,986 --> 00:16:21,445
Hey, quit laughing.

343
00:16:22,238 --> 00:16:23,447
[Taiki] I can't help it.

344
00:16:24,240 --> 00:16:25,533
[Chinatsu] Whatever.

345
00:16:25,616 --> 00:16:26,784
[Taiki] No, I'm sorry.

346
00:16:26,867 --> 00:16:27,952
[peaceful music ends]

347
00:16:28,869 --> 00:16:30,538
[birds chirping]

348
00:16:31,163 --> 00:16:33,916
{\an8}[Coach Yuasa] Everyone, congratulations
on entering your next year.

349
00:16:34,000 --> 00:16:35,918
While it may be a busy time of year,

350
00:16:36,002 --> 00:16:38,671
the national qualifiers
are just around the corner.

351
00:16:39,296 --> 00:16:41,382
You'll all face off in matches together.

352
00:16:41,465 --> 00:16:43,926
That'll determine who goes to qualifiers.

353
00:16:44,010 --> 00:16:44,927
[all] Yes, sir!

354
00:16:45,761 --> 00:16:48,180
We've got a long road ahead
to get to nationals.

355
00:16:48,264 --> 00:16:50,391
<i>First, get selected for the club's lineup,</i>

356
00:16:50,474 --> 00:16:52,810
<i>then get in the top 16 for regionals.</i>

357
00:16:52,893 --> 00:16:55,438
<i>After that, the top two
for prefectural qualifiers.</i>

358
00:16:56,230 --> 00:17:00,234
[Kyo] We have to at least beat Haryu,
who was third in the prefecture last time.

359
00:17:00,735 --> 00:17:02,069
[Taiki] If you reframe it,

360
00:17:02,153 --> 00:17:05,448
beating Haryu means we have
a chance at getting to nationals.

361
00:17:05,531 --> 00:17:06,949
That is a pretty clear goal.

362
00:17:07,867 --> 00:17:09,785
What are your stats up to now, by the way?

363
00:17:09,869 --> 00:17:10,703
Don't ask that!

364
00:17:12,455 --> 00:17:14,290
We have a larger crowd than usual.

365
00:17:14,373 --> 00:17:17,460
[Kyo] I bet a lot of them
are new to the school and observing.

366
00:17:18,085 --> 00:17:20,755
But, I think most of them
are probably here to watch.

367
00:17:22,298 --> 00:17:23,716
[all] Whoa!

368
00:17:24,675 --> 00:17:27,219
- Her fan base keeps growing every year.
- [grunts]

369
00:17:28,220 --> 00:17:31,223
And anyone who's not here
for her, is here to watch...

370
00:17:31,307 --> 00:17:32,808
[whimsical music playing]

371
00:17:34,060 --> 00:17:35,478
[all gasp]

372
00:17:36,771 --> 00:17:38,439
Just fantastic!

373
00:17:38,522 --> 00:17:39,482
Miss Chono!

374
00:17:39,565 --> 00:17:41,942
So wonderful. Beautiful. Fantastic!

375
00:17:42,026 --> 00:17:43,611
The star of the club!

376
00:17:43,694 --> 00:17:45,946
The one the gymnastic goddesses
smiled upon!

377
00:17:46,030 --> 00:17:49,033
You and me...
Let's make us number one in Japan!

378
00:17:49,742 --> 00:17:51,577
There's high hopes for that girl.

379
00:17:51,660 --> 00:17:54,789
[girl 1] I'm a senior,
but I feel like a nobody now.

380
00:17:54,872 --> 00:17:56,332
[girl 2] Wasn't she 4th in juniors?

381
00:17:56,415 --> 00:18:00,211
Her father was on the national team
for gymnastics, too, is what I heard.

382
00:18:01,003 --> 00:18:03,714
[girl 1] She really does seem
like the chosen one.

383
00:18:04,799 --> 00:18:06,592
It's 2,000 yen to watch me.

384
00:18:06,675 --> 00:18:08,219
I'm not paying that!

385
00:18:08,302 --> 00:18:10,763
I don't know, you were giving me
some intense looks.

386
00:18:10,846 --> 00:18:12,723
[Taiki] I wasn't giving you anything!

387
00:18:12,807 --> 00:18:15,017
I completely understand
that beautiful things

388
00:18:15,101 --> 00:18:16,477
are hard to look away from.

389
00:18:16,560 --> 00:18:18,229
[Taiki] Don't be so full of yourself!

390
00:18:18,312 --> 00:18:20,272
Why are you the way that you are!

391
00:18:21,565 --> 00:18:23,526
The gymnastics club is so cool.

392
00:18:23,609 --> 00:18:24,485
Yeah.

393
00:18:25,820 --> 00:18:26,821
Right, then!

394
00:18:26,904 --> 00:18:28,239
Back to practicing!

395
00:18:29,156 --> 00:18:30,032
Mm.

396
00:18:31,659 --> 00:18:34,954
[Taiki] <i>This isn't good.
She keeps seeing me with Hina like that.</i>

397
00:18:35,037 --> 00:18:37,248
<i>No wonder she has the wrong idea.</i>

398
00:18:39,625 --> 00:18:42,253
[giggles] Made ya look!

399
00:18:42,336 --> 00:18:44,338
Hina! Why are you here?

400
00:18:44,421 --> 00:18:46,048
Your house is the other way, right?

401
00:18:46,132 --> 00:18:49,176
Actually, there's a new clinic
in Azuma-cho,

402
00:18:49,260 --> 00:18:51,762
it's run by a famous chiropractor, apparently.

403
00:18:51,846 --> 00:18:54,390
I know it. My house is near...

404
00:18:54,890 --> 00:18:56,684
[gasps] <i>Hold on, uh-oh.</i>

405
00:18:57,351 --> 00:19:00,729
<i>If Hina sees Chinatsu,
going into the Inomata household...</i>

406
00:19:00,813 --> 00:19:02,231
[mischievous music playing]

407
00:19:02,314 --> 00:19:04,441
<i>Chinatsu should still be at school.</i>

408
00:19:04,525 --> 00:19:06,777
<i>I need to get Hina outta here, fast.</i>

409
00:19:07,528 --> 00:19:09,655
Let's get you there before it's busy.

410
00:19:09,738 --> 00:19:10,823
Okay then.

411
00:19:12,616 --> 00:19:13,784
- [Hina exclaims]
- Hm?

412
00:19:13,868 --> 00:19:16,036
- What a little cutie.
- Hey!

413
00:19:16,662 --> 00:19:18,539
You look just like Uncle Shuhei.

414
00:19:18,622 --> 00:19:21,667
[Taiki] <i>Stop saying things
no one understands but you!</i>

415
00:19:21,750 --> 00:19:23,919
- [dog pants]
- [Hina] Bye-bye.

416
00:19:24,003 --> 00:19:26,672
[Taiki] <i>She's the youngest child
and has type B blood. Typical.</i>

417
00:19:26,755 --> 00:19:27,673
PREJUDICED

418
00:19:28,299 --> 00:19:31,677
<i>Then again,
Hina doesn't understand the situation.</i>

419
00:19:31,760 --> 00:19:33,429
Oh, so good!

420
00:19:33,512 --> 00:19:34,972
[Taiki] <i>She's doing it on purpose.</i>

421
00:19:35,055 --> 00:19:36,307
Look, they have bean paste!

422
00:19:36,390 --> 00:19:37,308
TAIYAKI

423
00:19:37,391 --> 00:19:39,643
Okay, okay, I'll buy you one,
and then let's get going.

424
00:19:39,727 --> 00:19:40,561
[Hina] Huh?

425
00:19:40,644 --> 00:19:41,812
I'm good.

426
00:19:43,647 --> 00:19:44,690
Hina...

427
00:19:44,773 --> 00:19:46,400
Your face says otherwise.

428
00:19:46,483 --> 00:19:47,318
No, but...

429
00:19:48,110 --> 00:19:49,862
my daily calorie limit.

430
00:19:49,945 --> 00:19:50,821
I'll go over.

431
00:19:51,947 --> 00:19:53,365
It's all that sugar.

432
00:19:53,449 --> 00:19:55,326
If one has even just 40 grams, then...

433
00:19:55,409 --> 00:19:58,078
Is that how you think
about things every day?

434
00:19:58,662 --> 00:19:59,580
Of course.

435
00:20:00,414 --> 00:20:04,543
{\an8}Putting on just a few hundred grams...
that can make me move slower.

436
00:20:04,627 --> 00:20:07,880
{\an8}Then training in order to lose
that weight, it's a waste of time.

437
00:20:08,380 --> 00:20:10,799
{\an8}And I don't want
to get injured or hit a slump.

438
00:20:12,426 --> 00:20:15,512
Working hard isn't something
that I'm good at.

439
00:20:16,138 --> 00:20:18,599
If I can just grin and bear it,
then I'll do that.

440
00:20:20,935 --> 00:20:22,102
What's with your face?

441
00:20:22,186 --> 00:20:23,646
It's just...

442
00:20:23,729 --> 00:20:25,856
I was thinking that you're pretty cool.

443
00:20:25,940 --> 00:20:27,858
Well, that isn't what it looked like.

444
00:20:28,442 --> 00:20:32,613
{\an8}[Taiki] The fact that you can resist
taiyaki in the first place is impressive.

445
00:20:32,696 --> 00:20:33,614
[mellow music playing]

446
00:20:33,697 --> 00:20:36,075
But then you don't even see it as effort?

447
00:20:36,158 --> 00:20:38,369
It shows how disciplined you are
throughout your life.

448
00:20:39,411 --> 00:20:41,789
When I look at what "normal" is,

449
00:20:41,872 --> 00:20:45,584
what my normal is compared to the normal
of athletes much better than me,

450
00:20:45,668 --> 00:20:46,710
it makes me nervous.

451
00:20:47,544 --> 00:20:50,714
And then I see you
going for it alongside them.

452
00:20:51,632 --> 00:20:54,718
It makes me think
that you're so freaking cool!

453
00:20:58,305 --> 00:20:59,807
What is this?

454
00:20:59,890 --> 00:21:01,392
What's with all the feelings?

455
00:21:01,475 --> 00:21:03,852
Quit it! Don't act so chill after that!

456
00:21:05,062 --> 00:21:06,897
I'll never say it to you again.

457
00:21:09,942 --> 00:21:13,362
[Hina] But Mr. Taiki, I think
you're actually the cooler one.

458
00:21:13,445 --> 00:21:17,032
Finding the courage to talk to a girl
who's totally out of your league!

459
00:21:17,116 --> 00:21:18,742
[Taiki] You're making fun of me!

460
00:21:19,493 --> 00:21:22,663
If there is any assistance I can
provide you, my lord, say the word.

461
00:21:22,746 --> 00:21:23,664
I'll do it!

462
00:21:23,747 --> 00:21:25,499
Drop that character for starters.

463
00:21:25,582 --> 00:21:27,960
Even if you could help me
with this whole thing,

464
00:21:28,043 --> 00:21:29,753
there's nothing in it for you.

465
00:21:29,837 --> 00:21:31,255
Well, that may be true.

466
00:21:32,006 --> 00:21:35,634
But good sir, we should return
to the former topic of discussion!

467
00:21:35,718 --> 00:21:37,261
[Taiki] I'm not a "sir."

468
00:21:38,012 --> 00:21:40,347
Your courage
in surmounting this challenge,

469
00:21:40,431 --> 00:21:42,516
I think it's pretty cool, my lord!

470
00:21:42,599 --> 00:21:43,767
Whoosh!

471
00:21:44,560 --> 00:21:46,103
As your best friend,

472
00:21:46,186 --> 00:21:48,272
I want you to taste victory.

473
00:21:49,106 --> 00:21:51,692
Hina, why are you being so theatrical

474
00:21:51,775 --> 00:21:53,110
- all of a sudden?
- Huh?

475
00:21:53,193 --> 00:21:54,903
- Wait, what's going on?
- No, don't look!

476
00:21:54,987 --> 00:21:55,863
[exclaims]

477
00:21:59,533 --> 00:22:01,076
[Taiki] <i>It's Chinatsu and...</i>

478
00:22:01,994 --> 00:22:03,287
<i>Haryu?</i>

479
00:22:05,456 --> 00:22:07,458
[closing theme song playing]
